<% content_for(:title) { t("owner.restaurants.edit_title") } %>

<div class="admin-head">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
    <h1 class="admin-title"><%= t("owner.restaurants.edit_title") %></h1>
    <span class="admin-subtitle"><%= @restaurant.name %></span>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render "form", restaurant: @restaurant %>

<%# Below the form, and pointedly outside it. Everything in that form is a
    column on `restaurants`, saved to the server by the Save button and true for
    every device the account is signed in on. This is a localStorage flag on
    this one browser, written the instant it is pressed — dropped inside the
    form_with it would sit under a Save button with nothing to save for it, and
    would have taken effect already whether that button was pressed or not.

    Pressing it is also the point: a browser grants a document audio only inside
    a user gesture, so the control both records the preference and proves the
    device can be heard. That is why it is a button rather than a checkbox the
    form would submit.

    Same max-w-xl measure as the form, so the two read as one column. %>
<%# fieldset/legend rather than section/h2, to read as a third peer of Details
    and Service rather than as something bolted on underneath. Not only for the
    look: `.ledger-admin :is(h1, h2)` sets the body face and outranks
    `.form-section-title` — same layer, one component more specific — so an h2
    here silently loses the mono caps every other section title carries. A
    legend is what the form's own sections use, and it is announced as this
    group's label besides. %>
<fieldset class="form-section max-w-xl mt-8">
  <legend class="form-section-title mb-4"><%= t("owner.orders.sound.section_title") %></legend>

  <%# self-start: .form-section is a flex column, which would otherwise stretch
      the button across the whole measure. %>
  <%= render "owner/shared/sound_toggle",
             id: Owner::OrdersHelper::SOUND_TOGGLE_ID,
             class_name: "btn-wine-outline sound-toggle self-start",
             label_class: "" %>

  <p class="field-hint"><%= t("owner.orders.sound.device_hint") %></p>
</fieldset>
